          "sequenceIds": [
            "VSP_009271"
          ],
          "isoformSequenceStatus": "Described"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "value": "Each Drosophila eye is composed of 800 facets or ommatidia. Each ommatidium contains 8 photoreceptor cells (R1-R8), the R1 to R6 cells are outer cells, while R7 and R8 are inner cells. Rh6 is expressed in a subset of R8 cells, most likely expressed in the subset of R8 cells paired with Rh4-expressing R7 cells (R7y)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY"
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Phosphorylated on some or all of the serine and threonine residues present in the C-terminal region"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "PTM"
    },
    {
